  "reusable": true,
  "title": "Pre-Vote responses of an earlier round are accepted by a later round of the same term",
  "cause": "Engine::pre_elect builds every round from the unchanged local vote, so all rounds at one local term share the leader id (term+1, self); RaftCore::does_pre_candidate_vote_match compares only leader ids, and Candidate::grant_by expects the responder to be a voter of the current round.",
  "trigger": "A node starts a Pre-Vote round, starts another round at the same term (timer restart, trigger().elect(true), or after leader contact dropped the first), and a granted response to the first round arrives; for the panic, the responder was removed from the voter set between the rounds.",
  "consequence": "The grant is tallied by the wrong round: RaftCore panics (Fatal::Panicked) when the responder is no longer a voter, and otherwise a real election can start on grants the current round never received, inflating the term.",
  "sites": [
    "openraft/src/core/raft_core.rs:RaftCore::does_pre_candidate_vote_match",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:Engine::pre_elect",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:Engine::handle_pre_vote_resp",
    "openraft/src/proposer/candidate.rs:Candidate::grant_by"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "PreElect",
    "HandlePreVoteResponse",
    "SendPreVoteRequests"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "PreVoteStaleResponseIgnored",
    "PreVoteResponseNeverPanics"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "Two Pre-Vote rounds of one node can start at the same local term (timer restart after election_timeout, operator trigger().elect(true) without rate limit, or a new round after become_following dropped one).",
    "A granted response to the earlier round can be processed after the later round started (within the RPC ttl election_timeout_min, or queued as a notification).",
    "For the panic consequence, the responder is removed from the voter set between the rounds."
  ],
